Twist
=====

Copyright (C) 2026 Chris Burdess

Twist is a transfer client for the GNU system.  HTTP/1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3 are
implemented, and further schemes plug into the same transfer engine.
The command line is mostly compatible with curl's: the options, standard
streams and exit status are the same, so that twist can replace it in
scripts.

Dependencies
------------

  - quickstep, installed so that pkg-config can see quickstep.pc
  - foxtrot, the SSH engine, installed so that pkg-config can see foxtrot.pc
  - libgcrypt 1.12.4 or later, which foxtrot needs, and which the loader
    must find ahead of any older system copy (configure checks this)
  - zlib
  - GNU readline, for the twist program only

Build and install
-----------------

  ./bootstrap
  ./configure
  make
  make check
  make install

If quickstep is installed under a prefix pkg-config does not search,
pass that prefix:

  ./configure --with-quickstep=/prefix

The same applies to foxtrot, with --with-foxtrot=/prefix.

See INSTALL for the GNU build instructions, and TODO for what is
not yet implemented.

